    "text": "96\n\n Promissory Notes: Boring Name, Sexy Deal Tool\nHi Sara,\nIf you\u2019re buying or selling a business, you\u2019ve probably met our friend: the promissory note.\nSounds dull. It\u2019s anything but.\nA promissory note is a promise to pay. Groundbreaking, I know. But before you tune out, here\u2019s why it matters: when used right, it can make the difference between a deadlocked deal and one that gets across the finish line.\nHere\u2019s what you need to know\u2014without needing a law degree:\nYou want $1.2 million for your business. The buyer\u2019s stuck on $1 million. Enter: the promissory note. That extra $200K? It can live in a note, payable if the business performs post-closing. It\u2019s called a retention adjustment, and it\u2019s basically the deal version of \u201clet\u2019s see who\u2019s right.\u201d\nBut don\u2019t stop there.\nYou can slice and dice a note like a Vegas card shark. $500K note? Make $50K of it the SBA-required \u201cequity injection\u201d (hello, 24-month standby). Carve the rest into separate notes with different terms. The bank cares about how the equity portion of the Note is structured, but may have different (and more lenient) thoughts on the other parts.\nWhy I Like Notes More Than Earn-Outs if I\u2019m the Buyer\nEarn-outs are needy. They involve escrow agents, agreements, arguments, and fees. Notes? You just draft them, sign them, and boom\u2014you\u2019re off to the races. They\u2019re elegant. They\u2019re manageable. And they don\u2019t come with a customer service line.\nIf you\u2019re a busy business owner\u2014and most of my clients are\u2014this kind of simplicity matters. Notes let you build in conditional payments without the administrative circus of a full-blown earn-out. We love that.\n*But ON THE OTHER HAND, if I\u2019m the seller, I certainly like the fact that my money is sitting in an escrow account somewhere.\u00a0\nOne Last Note (Get It?)\nDon't treat notes like a monolith. Be strategic. Use multiple notes. Tailor the terms. And above all: stop pretending like \u201cstandard terms\u201d are your only option. You can (and should) get creative.\nWant help using deal tools that actually work?\nCheck out Deal Academy. It\u2019s the stuff they don\u2019t teach you in business school\u2014but maybe should.\nTo smarter structuring,\nSara Sharp\nPartner, SK&S Law Group\n\n For more helpful lessons from Deal Academy, check out our Dealmakers Youtube Channel where you'll find Sara's Weekly Wine Down, where she talks about what she's seen in the industry this week and interviews with M&A Experts and Dealmakers.\nYou can check out some recent Dealmakers YouTube videos by clicking the images below.\n\n Copyright \u00a9 2025\u00a0 Someday Consultants, All rights reserved. \n\n Our e-mail address is:\ninfo@dealacademy.org\n\n Want to change how you receive these emails?\n You can unsubscribe from this list.",
